# The Go toolchain is intentionally not a Build-Depends: Debian 12 and Ubuntu
# 22.04 ship a Go older than the "go" directive in go.mod requires, so the
# builder must provide its own (see debian/rules and packaging/build-debs.sh).

Package: ssh-gate
Architecture: any
# No ${shlibs:Depends}: the binary is linked with CGO_ENABLED=0 and has no
# shared library dependencies. init-system-helpers is Essential, so the
# deb-systemd-helper calls in the generated snippets need no dependency either.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ca-certificates
Description: SSH tunnel with SOCKS5 and HTTP proxy
 ssh-gate opens a single SSH connection to a gateway host and exposes local
 SOCKS5 and HTTP proxies over it. Per-destination direct routing rules decide
 which traffic bypasses the tunnel, and hostname resolution for tunnelled
 destinations goes through DNS-over-HTTPS queried over the same connection.
